{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Moses would take.</b> Future in place of past, in the manner of \"They made a calf at Horeb\" (Psalms 106:19)." "<b>The tent.</b> His [own] tent, like \"and they came to the tent\" (above 18:7)." "Now Moses was separated from Israel because of the Glory that would speak with him, and this was after he brought down the second tablets written, and Israel began to make the Tabernacle, and he called his tent \"Tent of Meeting,\" for HaShem would meet him there until the Tabernacle was made, and there is no earlier and later in the Torah. And some say that this is the tent of the Tabernacle, and Scripture told where the Tabernacle was before they set up the standards, the fifty days."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {2 "\"the fifty days\" is hyper-literal; the phrase is compressed and its precise referent is unclear, possibly the fifty days from the Exodus until the setting up of the standards."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:02.582864051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}